Develop Flipper Zero applications and firmware changes for an explicit firmware and SDK version. Verify API names and manifests against available headers; prefer public Furi and FuriHal interfaces, and identify firmware-specific dependencies. Account for stack, heap, GUI lifecycle, peripheral ownership, and persistent storage.

Pair allocations with frees and opened records with closes. Remove views before freeing them or their dispatcher. Signal worker threads to exit, unblock their waits, then join and free them; joining alone does not stop a worker. Keep long operations off the UI path and synchronize shared state deliberately.

For radio transmission, preserve band and region checks and handle transmission failure. Restrict security-sensitive peripheral operations to the authorized devices and testing scope; never bypass regional restrictions or support unauthorized access. Generate the required application manifest and use the target's supported build tools. Distinguish compilation, host tests, deployment, and on-device memory or peripheral checks; do not claim hardware verification from a successful build alone.
